.TH OMX-PANEL-STORE 1 "2026-11-20" "omx-panel" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-panel-store \- read and write the descriptions store of panel descriptions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-panel-store get
.BI --sha256 " H" " --format " F " --uri " U " --source " H
.RB [ --rules
.IR N ]
.B --json
.br
.B omx-panel-store put
.BI --sha256 " H" " --format " F " --uri " U
.br
.B omx-panel-store remove
.BI --sha256 " H" " --format " F " --uri " U
.br
.B omx-panel-store check
.br
.B omx-panel-store source
.BI --format " lv2|clap" " --path " P
.br
.B omx-panel-store places
.BI --production " user|system"
.br
.B omx-panel-store rules
.SH DESCRIPTION
The descriptions store holds a panel description per plugin in three files panel.sqlite: the base
(/usr/share/omx/panel/panel.sqlite, read only), the system layer (/var/lib/omx/panel/panel.sqlite) and the user layer
(~/.local/share/omx/panel/panel.sqlite). A reader takes the user layer, the system layer and the base, in that order;
root reads the system layer and the base only. The writer writes the layer of the effective uid: the system layer as
root, the user layer otherwise, never the base.
.PP
.B get
prints the entry of the plugin and the layer it came from as JSON, or null when no layer holds it; an entry made from
another source than
.B --source
is skipped as stale.
.B put
writes the entry read as JSON on standard input, and
.B remove
removes it.
.B check
opens every layer and prints ok or the refusal's code.
.B source
prints the source hash of an installed plugin, and
.B places
the files of a scope.
.B rules
prints OMX_PANEL_RULES_VERSION, the rules version a derived entry is put with and the reader holds current.
.PP
The command is a door of libomx-panel-store.so.0, which holds every rule. The schema a layer is created with is
compiled in; /usr/share/omx-panel-store/panel.sql, in the development package, is the same text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --scope " user|system" ", --base " F ", --system " F ", --user " F ", --contract-dir " D
the scope and the places, for a test; absent, OMX_PANEL_STORE_BASE, OMX_PANEL_STORE_SYSTEM, OMX_PANEL_STORE_USER and
OMX_CONTRACT_PATH, then the installed places
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (and for a get of a key no layer holds), 1 with the refusal's code (panel-store.*) on standard error, 2 on
a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omx-panel (1)
